**Effort feasibility note.** The 250-hour allocation to the Lead Developer equates to approximately 33 hours per week sustained across 19.5 weeks. This is achievable for a student team **only if the three-way parallel implementation split is eliminated**. At the time of audit, three separate client implementations existed simultaneously — two Flutter codebases and one React application. Ratifying ADR-001 and archiving the Flutter trees is therefore not merely an architectural preference; it is the precondition that makes the effort budget attainable. With three implementations in flight, 650 hours is insufficient; with one, it is sufficient with margin.

**Re-costing note.** The ₱11,600.00 and ₱183,500.00 figures, the 650-hour allocation, and the ₱8,000.00 tablet valuation were inherited unchanged from the Software Engineering I plan and carried forward through materially larger scope — through a front-end stack replacement, a schema expansion from six to nine tables, the addition of UUID idempotency and row-level locking, and a fourteen-scenario test matrix. The 33,900.00 hardware valuation also predates the expansion from one to three client tablets. These figures are retained here as the approved baseline but must be **re-costed upon approval of the nine-table scope**, and the re-costed schedule presented at gate G5.

