**CR-01 — Order Sync Non-Functional Due to Contract Incompatibility**

| Attribute | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Description** | Both client implementations transmitted a flat order map, while the backend required a nested `{"order": {…}}` envelope and rejected all such requests with HTTP 400. Neither client ever transmitted the `items` array the backend required. The observed effect was a 0% sync success rate: no order ever reached MySQL and no inventory was ever deducted server-side. |
| **Likelihood / Impact** | Certain (already realised) / Critical |
| **Consequence if realised** | The project's highest-priority client problem remains unsolved. Objectives 1, 2, and 6 all fail. The system would present as functional while silently discarding every transaction. |
| **Prevention** | The wire contract is frozen in §4.1 as a single normative artefact. Both the client envelope builder and the server parser are specified against it. Contract conformance is a gate condition at G4, G6, and G8, and is exercised continuously by scenarios T01–T08. |
| **Contingency** | Contract conformance is verified by a single end-to-end integration test executed before any other verification. If it fails, no other testing proceeds until it passes. |
| **Owner** | Zapico, Zaki (implementation); Gregorio, Rhea Mae (verification) |
| **Trigger / Indicator** | Any HTTP 400 or HTTP 422 response during a controlled sync test using a known-valid payload. |
| **Status** | **RESOLVED** by the Revision 2.3 contract and engine. |

---

**CR-02 — API Has No Authentication or Authorization**

| Attribute | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Description** | The predecessor backend performed no session validation, no role check, and no token verification, and emitted `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`. Any device that joined the hotspot — including a customer's telephone — could create orders, set an arbitrary `user_id`, and manipulate inventory. |
| **Likelihood / Impact** | Certain (already realised) / Critical |
| **Consequence if realised** | Inventory and revenue records are untrustworthy. Objective 7 and scenarios T10 and T11 cannot pass. The Data Privacy Act control promised in the Letter of Agreement is breached. Cash-handling accountability is impossible. |
| **Prevention** | Bearer-token authentication on every request, with only SHA-256 hashes stored in `api_sessions`. Session-derived user identity, so `user_id` is never accepted from the client. CORS restricted to the application origin. Every authorization denial written to `audit_logs`. |
| **Contingency** | If the token mechanism is unavailable, the endpoint is disabled entirely rather than operated unauthenticated. An open order-ingest endpoint on a shared hotspot is never an acceptable interim state. |
| **Owner** | Zapico, Zaki (implementation); Gregorio, Rhea Mae (verification) |
| **Trigger / Indicator** | Any successful POST to `sync.php` without a valid bearer token. |
| **Status** | **RESOLVED** by the Revision 2.3 engine; verified at gate G4. |

